body:
@CorneJB This should handle the various possible slices you may get. Since this did not occur for me in APR, would you mind checking if it passes the case that caused you trouble? I am assuming it was either missing git log, missing mailing list or both in a given time slice.

If this occurs in this new version, it will fill the data with NAs for the time window for the metrics it can't compute, and will compute the ones it can. 

Thanks!

I have made a few corrections to the concern on my previous comment to specify date times instead of commit hashes. The screenshot of the output has been accordingly updated, and the divergence on branches can now be observed on it. 

Furthermore, I got the chance to talk with @rnkazman today to clarify the approach, and we are good to go to move forward with the CLI for multibranch analysis.

@mumtaz-haris The ball is on your court unless another problem shows up when you try to run this for the other projects.
